# Complete multiple household tasks

Use a task list when setup has several independent parts that people cannot finish in one sitting. Simplify the task before adding a progress screen. These examples are local guidance. They do not add a Home Assistant screen, discover meters or enable an automation.

## Who owns what

Use [Ask clear questions on pages and in dialogs](question-pages.html#compose-the-task-without-replacing-its-owner) for each input and its retained answers. This page owns the progress view and the dependencies between tasks. The [Task list](../components/task-list.html) component owns the row presentation.

Opening or completing a documentation task must not enable an automation. Route to a real editor only when the installation provides one. Otherwise say the example is a reference.

## Use a small set of statuses

Use “Completed” and “Incomplete”. Add “Cannot start yet” only for a real dependency, and say what unlocks it. Keep a completed task open for correction. Show a task that cannot start as plain text, not as a link that does nothing.

